// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    The Drifter
// @category Character Tropes
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/The_Drifter
// @domain   Narrative
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): a rootless protagonist who blows into a troubled place a stranger, helps it
// for a time, and always leaves in the end — Campbell's Stranger archetype. The defining shape is the
// constellation of three: he arrives UNATTACHED ([+Stranger], belonging nowhere), he PROTECTS the
// locals against the thing draining their town, and then he DEPARTS — he does not stay, does not
// integrate, does not collect the reward. The discriminator is positive and event-bound: the SAME
// figure is the agent of both the Protecting and the Departing, and he carries [+Stranger]. That
// separates the Drifter from his neighbours — from The Mentor (who is [+Wise], bonds, and stays), from
// Found Family (who integrates rather than leaves), and from The Cavalry (who rescues but is no
// stranger). The leaving is the trope: help that arrives from outside and returns to it.

import "trl/tropes/character/roles/the_mentor.trl"   // the figure who STAYS and bonds — the Drifter's foil

// Lateral thematic links (optional, machine-followable — for discovery / embeddings).
assoc drifter -> [
  mentor : "is the leaving foil of (a stranger who departs, not a teacher who stays)"
]

// === ONTOLOGY ===
// The rootless helper: an outsider who protects and then withdraws, belonging nowhere.
imply Drifter -> [Stranger, Ally, Narrative]

// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// A [+Stranger] who PROTECTS a community and then DEPARTS from the place is The Drifter. The
// DISCRIMINATOR binds twice on the same figure: he is the agent of the Protecting AND the agent of the
// Departing, and he overtly carries [+Stranger] (the rootlessness that separates him from the mentor
// who stays). The leaving is required and positive — a Departs event, not the absence of a bond.
rule TheDrifter {
  when:
    char $drifter [+Stranger]
    set  $town [+Collective]
    evt  $aid [&Protected(agent=$drifter, other=$town)]
    evt  $leaving [&Departs(agent=$drifter, from=$place)]
  then:
    $drifter [+Drifter]
    $leaving [+Drifter]
}

// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Shane — the gunfighter who rides on (Western film, 1953) ===
// A lone rider drifts into a Wyoming valley a stranger and takes a hand's work on the Starrett
// homestead. When the cattle baron Ryker sets his hired gun on the homesteaders to drive them off
// their claims, Shane — who wanted only to hang up his guns — straps them on one last time, kills the
// gunslinger Wilson, and breaks the baron's grip on the valley. Then, wounded and unwilling to stay
// among the families he saved, he turns his horse back toward the mountains while the boy Joey cries
// after him. He protected them; he could not remain one of them. He rides on.

// SHANE — the lone rider; a stranger who belongs to no town
char shane [+Stranger] [+Protagonist]
shane [+Skilled]

// THE HOMESTEADERS — the troubled community he takes a hand to defend
set the_homesteaders [+Collective]

// RUFUS RYKER & HIS HIRED GUN — the cattle baron draining the valley, and the gunslinger Wilson
char ryker [+Antagonist] [+Authority]
char wilson [+Antagonist]

// THE VALLEY — the place he blows into and rides back out of
set the_valley [+Exterior] [+Day]

scene the_rider_passes {
  beat 1 {
    shane @ the_valley
    the_homesteaders @ the_valley
    // the threat: the baron sets his gun on the homesteaders
    ryker -- the_homesteaders : "Drives Them Off Their Claims"
    wilson -- the_homesteaders : "The Hired Gun"
  }
  beat 2 {
    // he protects them — straps the guns on one last time and breaks the baron's grip
    shane > wilson : "Outdraws The Gunslinger"
    evt the_stand [&Protected(agent=shane, other=the_homesteaders)]
    wilson [+Dead]
  }
  beat 3 {
    // and then he leaves — wounded, unwilling to stay among the families he saved, he rides on
    evt rides_on [&Departs(agent=shane, from=the_valley)]
        dialog(inject=[speaker=joey], inline="""
               speaker: "Joey"
               cue: "the boy running after the rider, the mountains ahead, the valley safe behind"
               tone: pleading, breaking
               text: "Shane! Come back!"
               """)
    // TheDrifter fires here: the [+Stranger] who Protected the [+Collective] town now Departs the
    // place. shane is DERIVED [+Drifter] and rides_on [+Drifter] — the leaving is the trope's payoff.
  }
}
